@startuml Perceptors navigation
' Every perceptor is a view of the endless sheet: its order. The server orders,
' the client lays out (the layout depends on the window width). Sections ride in the
' order stream; the side panel places them by the layout.

actor User
participant "Gallery /\nViewer" as Page
participant "SidePanel" as Panel
participant "wlayout\n(worker)" as Layout
database "layoutDb" as LDB
participant "gontroller\nAPI" as API
participant "Perceptor" as Nav
database "DB" as DB

== Start ==
Page -> API: GET /perceptors
API -> Nav: View()
API --> Page: [{slug, title, icon (SVG), help, relative}]
note right of Page: buttons: gallery toolbar\nand viewer toolbar;\nthe icon is a CSS mask\n(no script runs)
Page -> Layout: order(the URL's view: /v/<slug>?at=<guid>)
Layout -> LDB: the view's kept order, at once
Layout -> API: GET /p/:view/order?anchor=
API -> DB: shown items (Visible, Ready)
API -> Nav: Order(anchor, items)
Nav --> API: entries (guid, sections?)
API --> Layout: ndjson
note over Layout: the items are kept between visits\n(/items?since=: only the changes);\nthe server's order replaces the kept one\nonly if it differs
Layout -> LDB: items (x, y, order) + meta + sections (y)
LDB --> Page: visible window (liveQuery)
LDB --> Panel: section marks

== Switch in the gallery ==
User -> Page: perceptor button
Page -> Page: anchor = photo in the middle;\ngo to /v/<slug>?at=<anchor>
Page -> Layout: order(slug, anchor)
Layout -> API: GET /p/:view/order?anchor=
API --> Layout: entries
Layout -> LDB: relayout, meta.anchor = new position
LDB --> Page: window + scrollTo: the anchor stays in place

== Switch from the viewer ==
User -> Page: perceptor button (in the viewer)
Page -> Page: /v/<view>/<guid> replaced by\n/v/<slug>?at=<guid> (the viewer closes)
Page -> Layout: order(slug, the photo: centred)
LDB --> Page: the sheet around that photo

== Side panel ==
User -> Panel: scroll / point / drag
Panel -> Page: scrollTo(section position)
note right of Panel: unpinned: over the photos while scrolling;\npinned: always shown, the sheet makes room\n(a resize: the anchor keeps the view)
@enduml
